{"availability":"available","full":"eai-support/eai","name":"eai","description":"Enterprise AI CLI for scaffolding, configuring, and operating EAI vertical applications.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":2,"created":"2026-03-08T23:49:44Z","updated":"2026-10-16T07:04:23Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://eai-support.github.io/eai/","topics":["ai","cli","developer-tools","docusaurus","enterprise-ai","github-pages","gofer","typescript"],"demo":"https://eai-support.github.io/eai/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:21.117Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:21.117Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:21.117Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T02:04:56.644Z","stars":1,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-17T22:40:21.117Z","stars":1,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Scaffold, configure, validate, and operate EAI applications from a developer terminal.","The CLI gives teams a supported path for application setup, authentication, workspace selection, runtime validation, resource management, and deployment readiness. It keeps platform access behind authenticated commands and public-safe diagnostics, so developers and AI coding agents get useful next steps without exposing private infrastructure details.","Customer-facing CLI language uses workspace. The CLI also accepts the tenant command and --tenant- options for compatibility with existing scripts and platform API names. Stable fields such as tenantId, --tenant-id, limits.tenants, and role IDs such as tenant-admin remain unchanged. They refer to EAI workspaces or the platform role contract."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eai-support/eai/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9d73efb47a73d3579cc307b961183940cac8bd71dec5c92217f66bc6c38a2e99","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:21.251Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:21.251Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Scaff